+# Optional native clipboard bridge (X11 / Wayland)
+
+This proposal adds **an opt-in bridge** between the KMSCON Linux VT and
+one unprivileged desktop user session. It does **not** start a graphical
+clipboard service inside the privileged KMSCON process and does not
+require `xclip`, `wl-copy` or `wl-paste` at runtime.
+
+## Components
+
+- `src/clipboard_bridge.[ch]`: nonblocking Unix-domain socket client,
+  attached to the existing KMSCON event loop; timeouts and cancellation
+  are bounded. Clipboard operations are capped at 64 KiB and reject NUL.
+- `clipboard/x11/`: standalone user-session Xlib peer. Supports the
+  `CLIPBOARD` selection with UTF-8 text, a 1.5-second bound on an
+  unresponsive selection owner, and an isolated Xvfb recovery test.
+- `clipboard/wayland/`: standalone user-session Wayland peer using
+  `ext-data-control-v1`. Requires compositor support for this extension.
+- `Ctrl+Shift+C`: copies the existing mouse selection to the desktop
+  clipboard if a peer is configured; `Ctrl+Shift+V`: requests clipboard
+  text from that peer; if no peer is configured, invokes local selection
+  paste. The shortcuts ignore Caps Lock, but not unrelated modifiers.
+
+The ordinary middle-button local selection paste is retained.
+
+## Build the peers (independently of the KMSCON Meson build)
+
+From a KMSCON source tree that includes these changes:
+
+```sh
+make -C clipboard/x11
+make -C clipboard/x11 check        # requires Xvfb, Xlib and compiler
+make -C clipboard/wayland         # requires Wayland client, scanner,
+                                  # and wayland-protocols staging XML
+```
+
+KMSCON itself uses its existing Meson build; this patch adds the
+`clipboard_bridge.c` source to `src/meson.build`. Peer build integration
+with Meson and installation policy are left for upstream review, so that
+optional X11/Wayland dependencies are not forced on non-graphical builds.
+
+## Configuration and examples
+
+Run exactly one graphical peer as the **logged-in desktop user**:
+
+```sh
+# X11 example; path must be in a user-owned, private directory
+mkdir -p "$HOME/.cache"
+./clipboard/x11/kmscon-clipboard-x11 serve "$HOME/.cache/kmscon-clipboard-x11.sock"
+
+# Or Wayland (in a session supporting ext-data-control-v1)
+./clipboard/wayland/kmscon-clipboard-wayland serve     "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kmscon-clipboard-wayland.sock"
+```
+
+Then set `KMSCON_CLIPBOARD_SOCKET` to the **same socket path** in the
+KMSCON process environment, through the service manager or launch script.
+The socket belongs to the desktop user and must not be world-readable;
+KMSCON validates its peer credentials and the socket metadata. Peer
+failures do not block the KMSCON event loop indefinitely.
+
+**Limitations:** this is a local, trusted-user bridging arrangement.
+KMSCON running with elevated permissions can transfer clipboard text
+between the VT and the configured user session; do not point it at an
+untrusted socket or share the private socket directory. Wayland support
+is compositor-dependent. This contribution uses `ext-data-control-v1`,
+not the general Wayland clipboard protocol. X11 supports only bounded
+nonempty text, not arbitrary binary data or INCR transfers.
+
+## Upstream discussion points
+
+1. Decide whether to expose a documented config setting in addition to
+   the environment variable and whether to integrate peers into Meson.
+2. Confirm the authorship and licensing of the new peer source files;
+   they originate from the contributor's experimental source archives.
+3. Review security assumptions when the privileged KMSCON service
+   connects to an unprivileged user's socket.
+4. Review events around a late X11 `SelectionNotify` after a timeout.
+5. Test on X11 and additional Wayland compositors before general support
+   is advertised.
